contains a boulder or monster? Then the loader has to make some desicion 
what to do, but the loader shouldn't be concerned about such things, as 
they a pertinent to the game that saved the bones. And if you do it in 
the bones saver were back to those things that you deemed overly 
complicated.

You didn't address those things at all and I pointed that out.

There seems to be good reason why special levels are not eligible to 
bones and the reason is that no matter how you think you can do it, it 
becomes overly complicated.

[1] The game as it exist doesn't know which one of the two possible 
sokoban levels was loaded as there is no reason to know that after the 
level has been loaded and initialized. To save the knowledge somewhere 
that the bones saver can access it is and is not trivial. One can add 
global variables quite easily, but that's not good programing style as 
sooner or later the global variables start to hinder the normal namespace.

